Hi Mike, 

You are allowed to use the image in the publication. René kindly requests you acknowledge him in the following way:  René H.B. Fraaije, Het Nationaal Oertijdmuseum, NL. 

In terms of history: the cast was made in 1999 for Kirby Siber by the freelancer Aart Walen, to be used for expositions. Aart lacked space for the skeleton, so it was placed in Het Nationaal Oertijdmuseum in 2000, which significantly increased visitors. It was first placed in what is currently known as the 'sperm whale hall', but was placed in the large dinosaur hall which was being built in 2007. It was in that year the Het Nationaal Oertijdmuseum officially acquired the cast from Aart. 

As I said, the limb material is based on the 'Aurora' specimen from Spring Hill Quarry, Howe Ranch, WY, USA, but the exact nature of the cranial and axial casts is unknown to René, and it wouldn't surprise me - knowing Aart - that nobody exactly knows what is based on which specimen, but all material is based on SMA specimens. 

Let me know if you have any questions.

Cheers, 
Tom


